igned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "7fbd79a1-9017-5962-8464-c8335e25c404" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478470}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478483 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43596b54-0af5-56a0-a954-2be5f40712fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244900} {:answer/id #uuid "8b479d14-ade5-5b29-9efe-2745148ba46e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245536} {:answer/id #uuid "be780025-c235-58a6-8299-86b26eaeee98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246012} {:answer/id #uuid "e089e494-fe55-562d-9268-21868311ca66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246310} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c12ab0-ecc5-5590-8676-6569049bf30f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246374}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245536} :answer-field/id #uuid "03d089c3-601c-50be-8dc4-891bcf11d265" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f5c48c40-2fd0-5515-867f-1f3be83f3dfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-112656" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}+8{b}_{3} \\\\  & =8{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(4{b}_{3})+2{b}_{1}+2\\cdot 2(\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+4{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "9647de70-ff9d-5f4b-bc4e-14a190bb842f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478475}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478491 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "252cd9d2-cd28-51d0-86dc-f100bfbf8425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410020} {:answer/id #uuid "65ce31d1-a577-5b44-a7fa-3c3f399d7aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410028} {:answer/id #uuid "b63f4cd2-57fd-5205-92b4-a5bf14cc8ff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410040} {:answer/id #uuid "e15510ae-a912-51f2-b92f-d981d02b25f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410045} {:answer/id #uuid "fe8e8b08-4548-5fe8-adbd-3bce3207c85e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410050}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410028} :answer-field/id #uuid "de484491-607f-5712-bf20-9fe92c23a765" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "59ed1787-672a-57bb-b86d-43224b917d2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34772" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=-{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=4{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{b}_{1}+4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3} \\\\  & =4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3}-3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(3{b}_{2})+6(-{b}_{3})-\\frac{3}{4}(4{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}-\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$"} :step/id #uuid "c6f946eb-8d53-5f69-9732-0e531c296bb0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478481}}] :activity/title "Writing Vectors in Different Bases" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477731}]}
